+
+## Browser tools
+
+In browsers supporting [WebMCP](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/ai/webmcp/imperative-api),
+`open_search` and `open_reading_list` expose the header flyouts on every page.
+Their forms expose `search_articles`, `get_reading_list`, and a removal tool for each
+saved article. Article pages also expose `toggle_article_bookmark` when its button
+hydrates. Forms use the same submit handlers for users and agents, and return results
+through `SubmitEvent.respondWith()` for agent submissions.
+
+The four interactive articles register their own utility: `brew_coffee`,
+`get_tide_levels`, `get_plant_stats`, or `get_article_popularity` (requires `id`).
+Utilities return HTTP status, redirect details, and response bodies, preserving the
+sample APIs' intentional failures. Tools are removed on navigation or component
+unmount. Browsers without WebMCP retain the regular controls.
